 "Reading"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Writing"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Speaking"}]}, {"type": "post_instructions", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Instructions: Complete the following steps. Fill in the Self-Assessment."}]}]}]}], "type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Great Places to Visit"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "The Mysteries of Antarctica"}, {"type": "position", "content": 5}, {"type": "origin", "content": "scholar > Wining and Dining > How Spaghetti Came to Italy"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 15}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.1"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe routines and regular activities in a wider range of social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations"}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations"}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations"}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations"}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations"}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations"}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations"}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The Present Perfect Tense vs. The Simple Past Tense"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "To talk about the past, you can use the Simple Past and the Present Perfect."}, {"type": "text", "content": "For the Present Perfect tense, you think about the past and present together, because there is some connection between what happened in the past and now.<br/> <br/> For example:<br/> <ul><li><span class=\"italic\">Antarctica has always been a land of unexplored mysteries.</span> (It was a land of unexplored mysteries in the past, and it's a land of unexplored mysteries now.)</li></ul>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use the Simple Past tense to talk about a finished action or event not connected to the present. When we use the Simple Past, we use certain time expressions, such as: <span class=\"italic\">yesterday</span>, <span class=\"italic\">two days ago</span>, <span class=\"italic\">a month ago</span>, <span class=\"italic\">last Sunday</span>, <span class=\"italic\">in 1979</span>, among others.<br/> <br/> For example:<br/> <ul><li><span class=\"italic\">Over the years, scientific research replaced hunting wildlife.</span> </li></ul>"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":4,\"cells\":[\"\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Past tense form\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Past participle form\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"be\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"was\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"been\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Antarctica has always been ...</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"help\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"helped\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"helped\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Satellite pictures have helped ...</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"build\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"built\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"built\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Countries have built ...</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Antarctica has always been a land of unexplored mysteries.  "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Its size and shape were unknown until Captain James Cook sailed around the continent in 1770. "}, {"type": "example", "content": " Since then, satellite pictures have helped us build an accurate map of the whole continent."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Would Rather for What Is Preferable"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the expression <span class=\"italic\">would rather \u2026 </span>+ verb to express a preference. You can also use the contraction <span class=\"italic\">\u2018d rather ... </span> You use <span class=\"italic\">Would you rather \u2026 ?</span> to ask about someone's preferences."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">Would rather \u2026 </span> introduces a comparison between two options. You use this expression context clearly allows the subject to make a choice between one option or the other.<br>Example:<span class=\"italic\"> Would you rather visit Spain or Antarctica?</span><br><br>You use <span class=\"italic\">would rather</span> + <span class=\"italic\">than</span> to express a comparison between two things.<br>Example: <span class=\"italic\">I would rather explore the world than work in an office.</span><br><br>When the subjects are different, you use <span class=\"italic\">would rather</span> + <span class=\"italic\">Past Simple.</span><br>Example: <span class=\"italic\">I'd rather you didn't go out tonight.</span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "The scientists would rather find ways to improve the world. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "They'd rather use Antarctica for peaceful activities than for hunting seals."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "unexplored "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "an area not investigated or mapped "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Antarctica has always been a land of unexplored mysteries."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le15ob05aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to talk about a mysterious place!"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "unknown "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "not familiar; secret "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The shape of Antarctica was unknown until James Cook sailed along its shoreline in 1770."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le15ob05aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "satellite"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " a device that orbits the earth in order to collect information"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Satellite pictures have helped us build a map of Antarctica."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le15ob05aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "accurate "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "correct in all details; exact "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The pictures provide an accurate map of Antarctica."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le15ob05aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "continent "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a large, continuous expanse of land "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Antarctica is the only continent that is entirely covered in ice."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le15ob05aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "ozone layer "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the part of the earth's atmosphere that absorbs most of the Sun's radiation "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Scientists are trying to find out more about the hole in the ozone layer."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le15ob05aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "peaceful "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "not seeking war or violence "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Scientists would rather use the continent for peaceful activities."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le15ob05aud07"}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn6le15ob05re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Go online and find information about a famous explorer."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Who was it?"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Find out where they traveled to and how they got there. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Find out what they discovered. For example, did they discover a new unexplored territory? Another group of people? "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Find out how they changed the world that we know."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write a presentation (12-14 lines) and share it with your partner."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I write about natural wonders."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write about famous explorers."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write about events in the past."}]}]}